sho-metrics-source-linux (0.3.0+linux4-0ppa1~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix a restart loop on machines without lactd. The unit waited 90s for
    /run/lactd.sock, exactly systemd's default TimeoutStartSec, so where the
    socket never appeared start-pre was killed and Restart=on-failure looped
    the unit forever. The wait is now gated on lactd being configured, and
    TimeoutStartSec is raised above it.

 -- Emanuele Sparvoli <sparvoli@gmail.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:40:00 +0100

sho-metrics-source-linux (0.3.0+linux3-0ppa1~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Stop enabling the user service for every account on the machine.
    debhelper picked the unit up from the install tree and had the postinst
    run deb-systemd-helper --user enable, which the Arch and Fedora packages
    do not do. It is now installed disabled, like the other two.
  * Keep server.mjs executable, matching its shebang.

 -- Emanuele Sparvoli <sparvoli@gmail.com>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:05:12 +0100
